Research: .collab/research/2026-10-16-t3-code-c2c-support.md and live receipt JSON. Quality: preserve existing codebase architecture; small typed interfaces; meaningful regression and failure tests; no mock-only delivery claims; no whole-tree refactor; independent review/fix loop before merge. Decisions and evidence must be appended through bl. Implement canonical OCaml support needed by T3 to bind stable host-managed identity, inspect message envelopes and acknowledge only selected durably accepted IDs. Existing proven primitives should be reused. Regression tests cover malformed/untrusted IDs, concurrent arrival, repeat ack, namespace isolation, DND/flags, restart, and existing clients. Do not start or inject into a provider behind T3.